    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6734" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cărambis</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cēr-</span></b> ), is, f.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κάραμβις</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a promontory and town of the same name in
				Paphlagonia</i>, now <i>Kerempi Bukna</i>, or <i>Kerembeh</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 19,
				8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 2, 2, § 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Val. Fl. 5,
				107</span></i>; acc. Carambin, <i><span class="en">id. 8,
				214</span></i>.—<i>Adj.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cărambĭcus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 1, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 12,
				26, § 86</span></i>.</div>
